What positions are typically occupied by the players on the field in an AFL game?
According to the provided context, the positions typically occupied by the players on the field in an AFL game are:

1. Forward line (6 players, arranged into two lines of three players each)
2. Back line (6 players, arranged into two lines of three players each)
3. Midfield (players who either stay in the centre area of the ground or follow the ball and are not confined to a particular area)

Note that the modern game has largely discarded positional play, and most players have a specialist position and one or two "fill-in" positions.
