According to Major League Baseball (MLB), a "no-hit" game, also known as a no-hitter, is defined as a completed game in which a team that batted in at least nine innings recorded no hits. A pitcher who prevents the opposing team from achieving a hit is said to have "thrown a no-hitter". This is officially recorded when a pitcher (or pitchers) allows no hits during the entire course of a game, which consists of at least nine innings.
