Car manufacturers typically handle the transition from old to new models by introducing new models in phases, often around the world, and introducing facelift versions of existing models to attract new and past customers. The overlap period between old and new models can last for 2-3 years, during which time the company may push out a facelift version to maintain market share. The new model is often launched in the fourth quarter of the preceding year, coinciding with the launch of the traditional new television season in late September, to take advantage of heavy advertising and promotional activities.
