What is the origin and history of area codes in the United States, specifically focusing on the 951 area code?
The origin and history of area codes in the United States can be briefly summarized as follows:

Area codes were created as part of the North American Numbering Plan (NANP) by AT&T and Bell Laboratories in 1947. The plan was designed to provide a standardized system for assigning phone numbers across the United States and Canada.

Regarding the 951 area code specifically, it was split from area code 909 on July 17, 2004. Prior to that, the area covered by 951 was part of area code 714 until November 14, 1992. This makes the 951 area code the last new area code in California to have been split from another one, as all subsequent area codes introduced in the state have been overlays.
