The original Broadway production of "Kiss Me, Kate" opened on December 30, 1948, at the New Century Theatre, where it ran for nineteen months before transferring to the Shubert Theatre, for a total run of 1,077 performances. A revival production opened at the Beck Theatre on November 18, 1999, and closed on December 30, 2001, after 881 performances and 28 previews.
